      "title": "United Airlines says ‘widespread’ system outage resolved",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/nov/16/united-airlines-system-outage",
      "description": "<p>Airline acknowledges ‘technology issue that delayed flight departures’ in latest high-profile outage to affect Americans</p><p>United ⁠Airlines said on ⁠Monday ⁠that it had resolved ⁠a widespread system ⁠outage, just three days after the Federal ⁠Aviation Administration issued a rare nationwide ground stop on all US flights.</p><p>“We have resolved a technology issue that delayed flight departures. While some flights were delayed, there was no impact on flights in progress, or on United Express flights,” Chicago-based United said in a statement. “There is no indication that this was a cybersecurity-related issue.”</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/nov/16/united-airlines-system-outage\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-11-17T02:57:06"
    },
    {
      "title": "United Airlines resolves tech issue that delayed flights across US",
      "link": "https://www.business-standard.com/world-news/united-airlines-resolves-tech-issue-that-delayed-flights-across-us-126111700042_1.html",
      "description": "United Airlines said Monday that it had resolved a technology issue that delayed departing flights, just days after a malfunction in the Federal Aviation Administration's network prompted a nationwide ground stop.\nChicago-based United said in a statement that while some flights were delayed because of the issue Monday afternoon, flights that were in the air and flights on its United Express regional network were not impacted. It also said, \"There is no indication that this was a cybersecurity-related issue.\"\nUnited apologised to customers for the inconvenience on social media.\nA recording posted on the ATC app showed a United pilot in Houston asking the tower for permission to stay put at the gate until the system was working again. The app combines live air traffic control radio feeds with real-time visual aircraft tracking.\nThe flight tracking website FlightAware showed United with 418 delayed flights late Monday afternoon.\nThe United computer problem is just the latest high-pro",
      "source_name": "Business Standard Latest",
      "published": "2026-11-17T02:17:55"
    },
